# A lambda-omega system of docs/design/isochrons.md (test 2):
# r' = r(1-r^2), theta' = w + q(1-r^2) in Cartesian coordinates. The cycle is
# r = 1 with period 2*pi/w; the asymptotic phase is (theta - q ln r)/w, so
# for q != 0 the isochrons are logarithmic spirals.
par w=1,q=1.5
g=1-x^2-y^2
om=w+q*g
x'=x*g-y*om
y'=y*g+x*om
init x=1,y=0
@ total=60,dt=0.01
done
